  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Boil the kettle. Peel potato and cut into large chunks.\n• Half-fill a medium saucepan with boiling water.\n• Cook potato in boiling water, over high heat, until easily pierced with a fork, 12-15 mins.\n• Drain and return to saucepan. Add the milk and 1/2 the butter and season generously with salt. Mash until smooth.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/693119797558b9c7de4dcb14/step-859c2100.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, cut capsicum into bite-sized chunks. Finely chop or crush garlic. Thinly slice spring onion (see ingredients). Drain and rinse lentils.\n• Finely chop brown onion (see ingredients).\n• Heat a drizzle of olive oil in a large frying pan over medium-high heat. Cook capsicum, onion and lentils until tender, 2-3 mins.\n• Add Mexican Fiesta spice blend (use less if you’re sensitive to heat!), garlic and tomato paste and cook until fragrant, 1 min. Stir in the water, stock powder and remaining butter, then cook until slightly thickened, 3-4 mins.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/693119797558b9c7de4dcb14/step-3ef9ca10.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Preheat grill to high. Remove frying pan from heat and season to taste.\n• Transfer lentil filling into the baking dish. Spread mash evenly over the top.\n• Sprinkle with Cheddar cheese and grill until lightly golden, 8-10 mins.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/693119797558b9c7de4dcb14/step-faeb3e20.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Divide Mexican lentil pie between plates. Dollop with Greek-style yoghurt.\n• Sprinkle over spring onion to serve.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/693119797558b9c7de4dcb14/step-7ba90f30.jpg"
    }
  ]
}
